  "purpose": "R9-D root-cause diagnostic for the post-R29 carveout_sensitivity_probe L1-head divergence. Captures the upstream pipeline state (classifier manifest match counts, per-PC trace omissions, per-threadblock record counts, walker outputs) so the responsible subsystem can be isolated definitively before the production fix lands.",
  "root_cause_classification": {
    "class_a_classifier_manifest_filter_gap": {
      "evidence": "Trace contains 930 unique PCs but the classifier manifest contains only 25 PCs; 905 PCs in the trace are NOT in the manifest, and the omitted records total 1623168. Root cause is the _PC_RE regex in tools/cache_predictor/l1_cache_op_classifier.py which requires the PC literal to start with 0: the pattern is '0x?([0-9a-fA-F]+)' which is literal-0 then optional-x then hex, instead of the intended '(?:0x)?([0-9a-fA-F]+)'. With the old binary, this happened to match all 26 LDG.E PC strings (all started with 0x0); on the new binary, many PCs are above 0x1000 and do NOT start with 0, so they fall out of the manifest.",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "class_b_trace_adapter_dedup_bug": {
      "evidence": "Per-block instruction counts are uniform (25768/block, 406 L1-eligible/block under the old classifier). Adapter is producing records consistent with the classifier-filtered PC set.",
      "status": "ruled_out"
    },
    "class_c_walker_model_under_counting_reuse": {
      "evidence": "After applying the class-A fix locally and regenerating predicted_l1, carveout's predicted_hit_rate moved 0.0052 -> 0.0010 (further AWAY from NCU truth 0.9751), and register_spill_local_mem moved from typed_unavailable -> 0.0683 (NCU truth 0.9682) rather than improving. The new classifier admits the L1-eligible records, but the walker still does not capture the intra-block reuse pattern that NCU measures via multi-launch warmup. Walker hit/miss accounting requires the class-A fix AND a separate fix in the per-SM line-level LRU / set-associative model OR a multi-launch warm-cache simulation.",
      "status": "confirmed_as_secondary"
    },
    "class_d_cta_scheduling_capacity_mismatch": {
      "evidence": "Effective L1/shared carveout capacity in evidence_unified_budget_bytes=131072 matches the post-R29 max_carveout_max_l1 + shared allocation; per-block dispatch is uniform across 64 blocks; per-SM partitioning is consistent with the documented sm_86 SM count.",
      "status": "ruled_out"
    },
    "production_fix_path": "Both class-A and class-C must land together in a single round per BL-20260509 bounded-scope discipline. Landing class-A alone cascade-fails the focused suite (register_spill_local_mem regresses + 4 task12_substitution_preflight tests break under regenerated predicted_l1). R14 captures the diagnostic + repairs the xfail regression test signature; R15+ lands the combined production fix."
  },
